{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["And Moshe said to Aharon — Do not mourn, do not weep, and do not cease from the service, for this thing that I am telling you: it is what YHWH spoke: 'Through them that are near Me I will be sanctified' — through the high priests who are near Me to serve Me, I wish to be sanctified, and not that My name and My service be profaned. For thus the Holy One, blessed be He, said to me: ״והכהן הגדול מאחיו וגו׳ את ראשו לא יפרע ובגדיו לא יפרם״, ״ומן המקדש לא יצא ולא יחלל את מקדש אלהיו״ — behold, if he does not go out, he has sanctified. And there is no earlier and later in the Torah, and therefore do not leave the service, for you are a high priest and you must not go out and must not profane; rather, let the Holy One, blessed be He, and His service be sanctified through you." "'And before all the people I will be honored' — this is the glory of the Shekhinah, that He sees his sons dying and he sets aside his mourning for the service of his Creator." "'And Aharon was silent' — from his mourning; he did not weep and did not mourn. For thus it is written in Ezekiel: ״בן אדם הנני לוקח ממך את מחמד עיניך במגפה וגו׳ האנק דום מתים אבל לא תעשה״." "So too here, 'and he was silent' — from what he would have wanted to mourn and to weep. And this is instruction and the truth of its plain sense. But the aggadah that says: that Moshe was comforting Aharon, because the Holy One, blessed be He, had said to him: ״ונקדש בכבודי״ — and you supposed, either I or you; now you know that they are greater than me and you — this is not according to the plain sense. For would the Holy One, blessed be He, have said to Moshe: 'Make Me a sanctuary' — and on that very day the greatest among you will die?!"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:36.123185296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}